FINAL ANSWER:
**Ask Troy Goode to review it.** They wrote most of `lib/index.js`, and they're the only owner who has committed to it in the past year. But that answer depends on an unconfirmed guess about their two email addresses.

**The two addresses.** Troy Goode commits as `<email redacted>` and as `troy@laptop.example`. The tool guesses these are one person from the matching name and rates the guess strong, but it hasn't been confirmed and I haven't merged anything in `.mailmap`.
- **If they're one person:** they hold 144 non-blank lines (67.3%) of `lib/index.js`, or 159 counting blank lines (66.8%). Their last commit to the file was 2026-04-10, under the laptop address.
- **Counted separately, in `lib/index.js`:**
  - `<email redacted>`: 132 non-blank lines (61.7%), 147 counting blank lines (61.8%). Last commit to this file was 2016-08-23 (inactive).
  - `troy@laptop.example`: 12 non-blank lines (5.6%), 12 counting blank lines (5.0%). Last commit was 2026-04-10 (active).
- **Counted separately, across the whole repo:** `<email redacted>` has 605 non-blank lines (36.4%) and `troy@laptop.example` has 44. Together that would be 649 lines (39.0%).

If the laptop address isn't really the same person, no active owner of this file is left. `--identities` prints the `.mailmap` line that would make the merge permanent, once you confirm it.

**Owners in order of surviving lines (`--reviewers lib/index.js`):**

| Owner | Non-blank lines | Counting blank lines | Last commit to this file | Active? |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode, `<email redacted>` | 132 (61.7%) | 147 (61.8%) | 2016-08-23 | no |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 20 (9.3%) | 22 (9.2%) | 2017-10-04 | no |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades (also shows up as `alex94puchades`) | 14 (6.5%) | 16 (6.7%) | 2015-05-28 | no |
| Troy Goode, `troy@laptop.example` | 12 (5.6%) | 12 (5.0%) | 2026-04-10 | yes |
| LuisEGR | 6 (2.8%) | 6 (2.5%) | 2021-07-20 | no |
| 20 more authors | | | | |

- **Douglas Christopher Wilson** is the clear second owner, but they've stopped working on this file and on the project. Their last commit anywhere in the repo was 2021-09-07, so they probably can't be reached for a review.
- **No active second reviewer exists.** No one else active owns any of this file.
- **Bus factor is 1.** Bus factor is the fewest people who together hold half the lines. The gmail address alone holds 61.7% of the 214 non-blank lines (61.8% of the 238 counting blank lines), and it takes 4 people to reach 80%. "Active" means a commit in the year before 2026-04-12, the date of the latest commit. By that measure 1 of 18 authors is active, holding 67.3% of the lines. The other 32.7% belongs to people with no commit in that year.
- **Orphaned code:** none.

**What affects these numbers:**
- **Reformat commit left out:** the latest commit, 62628c0 ("style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes"), only changed formatting: 1,016 lines in 4 files. Those lines go back to the people who wrote them. Without that correction, the gmail address would hold 132 lines (61.7%) → 111 (51.9%).
- **Another possible mechanical commit, kept in:** fcd2b56 ("switch to ESLint; clean up") by Troy Goode, with 5 surviving lines. It isn't large enough to change the ranking.
- **Committer vs. author:** 11 lines of e64e854 are credited to their author, Alejandro Caravaca Puchades; Troy Goode only committed them. Likewise, 6 lines of f038e77 are credited to LuisEGR; Douglas Christopher Wilson only committed them.
- **History starts at an import:** the history begins with an import on 2013-01-30, so anything older is credited to whoever imported it. Merge commits are credited to the authors of the merged branches.
- **Method:** the counts come from `git blame -w -M -C`. They show whose lines are still there, not who understands the code best.

Once your change is committed, run `surviving-lines --for-diff main...HEAD`. It counts only the lines you actually replace or delete, which may point to someone other than the file's overall owner. New lines you add won't count toward anyone, because they had no earlier owner.
